{"recall":{"defs":[["Logistic regression","Linear model of the log-odds; outputs σ(θᵀx)."],["Decision region","Part of input space assigned to one class."],["Cross-entropy","Negative log-probability of the true class."],["Confusion matrix","Counts of TP, FN, FP, TN."],["ROC curve","TPR vs FPR over all thresholds."],["One-vs-rest","One binary classifier per class; pick the most confident."]],"formulas":["h_\\theta(x)=\\frac{1}{1+e^{-\\theta^\\top x}}","J(\\theta)=-\\tfrac1m\\sum\\left[y\\log h+(1-y)\\log(1-h)\\right]","\\tfrac{\\partial J}{\\partial\\theta_j}=\\tfrac1m\\sum(h-y)x_j","p(\\text{mistake})=\\int_{\\mathcal R_1}p(x,\\mathcal C_2)dx+\\int_{\\mathcal R_2}p(x,\\mathcal C_1)dx","\\text{P}=\\tfrac{TP}{TP+FP},\\ \\text{R}=\\tfrac{TP}{TP+FN},\\ F_1=\\tfrac{2PR}{P+R}","\\text{FPR}=\\tfrac{FP}{FP+TN}"],"takeaways":["Choose the class with the largest posterior; overlap sets the irreducible error.","Logistic regression = sigmoid of a linear score; boundary θᵀx = 0.","Cross-entropy is convex and its gradient is (h − y)x.","Accuracy misleads with imbalance; use precision, recall, F1 and ROC/AUC.","Costs decide thresholds; multi-class via one-vs-rest or one-vs-one."],"confused":[["Precision vs recall","Correctness of flags vs coverage of positives."],["Specificity vs FPR","TN rate vs 1 − TN rate."],["sklearn C vs α","C = 1/α."],["ROC vs PR curve","TPR vs FPR (skew-insensitive) vs precision vs recall (skew-sensitive)."],["Logit vs logistic","log(p/(1 − p)) vs 1/(1 + e^(−z)): inverses."]],"minute":"Classification assigns the class with the highest posterior; regions where classes overlap produce unavoidable error. Logistic regression models P(y = 1|x) = σ(θᵀx), so the boundary is θᵀx = 0 and each coefficient multiplies the odds by e^θ. It is trained by minimising convex cross-entropy with gradient descent, whose update (h − y)x matches linear regression's. Evaluate with the confusion matrix: precision, recall, F1, specificity and FPR, plus ROC/AUC across thresholds. With rare classes, avoid accuracy, rebalance training data and tune the threshold. For many classes use one-vs-rest or one-vs-one."},"flashcards":[["Bayes decision rule","Choose the class with the largest posterior p(C|x)"],["Generative vs discriminative","Model p(x|c)p(c) vs model p(c|x) or boundary"],["Sigmoid","$g(z)=\\frac1{1+e^{-z}}$, $g'=g(1-g)$"],["Logistic hypothesis","$h_\\theta(x)=\\frac1{1+e^{-\\theta^\\top x}}$"],["Log-odds","$\\ln\\frac p{1-p}=\\theta^\\top x$"],["Decision boundary","$\\theta^\\top x=0$ (h = 0.5)"],["Cross-entropy","$J=-\\frac1m\\sum[y\\log h+(1-y)\\log(1-h)]$"],["Logistic GD update","$\\theta_j\\leftarrow\\theta_j-\\alpha\\frac1m\\sum(h-y)x_j$"],["Odds ratio","$e^{\\theta_j}$ per unit increase in $x_j$"],["sklearn C","Inverse regularisation strength"],["Precision / recall","TP/(TP+FP) / TP/(TP+FN)"],["F1","2pr/(p + r)"],["FPR / specificity","FP/(FP+TN) = 1 − TN/(TN+FP)"],["ROC landmarks","(0,1) ideal; diagonal random; AUC 1 perfect, 0.5 random"],["OvR vs OvO count","K models vs K(K−1)/2"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["c-decision"],"viz":["rocThreshold"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["c-types"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3","why"],"deep":["c-ls"],"viz":["lsVsLogit"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["c-sigmoid"],"viz":["sigmoidLab","logitTrainer"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["c-cost"],"viz":["logitTrainer"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6","demo"],"deep":["c-gd"],"viz":["logitTrainer"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7","example"],"deep":["c-apply"],"viz":["sigmoidLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["c-reg"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8"],"deep":["c-eval"],"viz":["confusionLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["c-which"],"viz":["confusionLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h10"],"deep":["c-roc"],"viz":["rocThreshold","rocBuilder"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["c-imbalance"],"viz":[],"status